          "source_offset_encoding": "UNICODE_CODEPOINTS_IN_UTF8_SIG_DECODED_IMMUTABLE_SOURCE",
          "source_slice_sha256": "ae050f3f60ed7a12b2c3cc027ff46ca3cc8becf550f1371257014273471f8db6",
          "source_start": 11563,
          "source_text": "In 1931, G\\\"odel proved the two ``incompleteness theorems,'' which\r\nshowed that this program could not succeed. There is no axiom system\r\nfor mathematics which is complete, specifically, the sentence that\r\nexpresses the consistency of the axioms is a sentence which can\r\nneither be proved nor refuted."
